A||||12||3fifty||Dash Lights||||3||
Z||000000||3fifty||02-06-2001||12:28 AM||||I have an 86 GT. The dash lights are real dim. Even with the reostat turned all the way up. Is this a common problem? Can you <BR>boost the power to the lights, or is there<BR>a different color bulb that is a direct replacement? The blue in my F-150 looks great. The white face guages are out, because I have the 85mph speedo.<P>Thanks,<BR>350 one day!!!!!||||reg||3
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||02-06-2001||01:21 AM||||I would try removing the bulbs and cleaning them off. Sounds like they are dusty!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Vlad||02-06-2001||01:35 AM||||Check for good connection in negative terminal of the battery. There is a small wire grounded to the battery tray. That may be the reason of your trubles.||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||02-06-2001||04:03 AM||||also, there is a transister in the dimming circuit - located on a heatsink under the dash to the right of the steering column.....I have seen those go out and when beginning to go out the lights will not respond to the dimming rheostat.......||||reg||1
Z||000004||Rodney||02-06-2001||08:56 AM||||I have bright bulbs for the early style gauges. They are about twice as bright as the original bulbs but the gauges will not be twice as bright. But it will be better. $10 for a set of 7 and $2.00 shipping. Not on my web page yet. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Steven||02-06-2001||09:50 AM||||Hey Rodney, I have seen in the past where people put a brighter light bulb in something and the brighter bulb put out more heat, and warped the plastic. Now when ever I have seen this, it was in a tail lamp, but I guess I am wanting to know, are you brighter bulbs hotter to the point that it will over heat the plactic parts of my cluster?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Rodney||02-06-2001||10:59 AM||||These are not hot enough to do damage. I have several test sets out for several weeks now and they have reported no damage. These do run hotter but not enough to do any damage. I felt they would be OK but did some tests to be sure first. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Steven||02-06-2001||11:17 AM||||Man, I love it when people, like you Rodney, have already done the research, and are ready for question. Keep up the great work, and I will be order them once I have my ride back on the road.||||reg||1
Z||000008||MikeSchaefer||02-06-2001||11:29 AM||||Rodney, how many lights are needed to replace all of them behind the dash?  Probably 7, just makin sure.  Oh, are you gonna come to the El Paso IL show again this year?  I'd love to have you again.  Details can been seen here: <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/1930/elpasoshow.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/1930/elpasoshow.html</A> <BR>Later,<BR>Mike Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Rodney||02-06-2001||11:49 AM||||It takes 7 bulbs for the illumination. The rest are indicator lights etc..<P>Not sure if I'll make the show again this year. There is a good chance I will make it. Not absolutely sure at this time though. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||sqoach||02-06-2001||12:44 PM||||hey rodney, do you have the blue lightbulbs for the gauges also? if not, do you know a place that sells them, or can i find some just about anywhere?<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||theogre||02-06-2001||07:07 PM||||Before changing bulbs, you need to check the dimmer transistor. This is under the dash. There is an article in my cave about it. <A HREF="http://fierocave.shorturl.com" TARGET=_blank>The Ogre's Fiero Cave</A> This article tells you how to repair it or replace it. The transistor is cheap and plentifull.||||reg||1
Z||000012||2xsess||02-06-2001||10:24 PM||||Well, I have been testing these in my dash and in the side marker lights for about a month. No warpage or and other deformations.<BR>The dash lights work so awesome with the white face gauges I got. With the stock faces on the gauges the regular bulbs were ok but with these i can only imagine how bright they would be. <P><BR>I'd give this two thumbs up!!<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2xsess.gif">    <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html</A>||||reg||1
